 :lessons
 ["A control is only a control when the thing it controls is otherwise green.
   The first version of the table gate's control fired 'cannot go red' on an
   already-red base and said the opposite of the truth."
  "Two build scripts, one pin each, and the stale one fails with a message
   about TYPED VALUES rather than about the pin. The control that settled it
   was building the UNMODIFIED tree with the same script: it failed
   identically, so the rejection was never about the new code."
  "`git push -q ... | tail` reports tail's exit. Measured again today; the
   push was fine, but the reading was not. Write to a file, take $?, then
   read -- the same class the AGENTS.md names."
  "A python -c patch that asserts before it writes leaves the file untouched
   and the next command reports success about the OLD content. It happened
   twice today and both times the give-away was a print line that still had
   the old shape."
  "The relay was finished weeks ago and the board implemented none of it. A
   protocol with one end written is indistinguishable from a working one until
   somebody sends a real request: every log on both sides read healthy."]}
